        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-04T23:39:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It comes from a joke that I used to tell a bunch and people got tired of hearing it. So I put it in a game so that people had to hear it over and Over and OVER AND OVER!</p><p>Many people here who have met me know that I can be a bit bossy and demanding... sure, we'll go with that. Anyway, if accused of telling others what to do or how to do it, I would often respond by telling a long and involved story of when I went to the doctor to get stitches and how I spent the entire time correcting the doctor's methods until the doctor exasperatedly threw the needle and thread at me, yelling, \"Fine! Suit yourself!\"</p><p>(If you still don't get it, say it out loud.)</p><p>At this point, my audience realizes the entire story is a joke and groans at both how much time I spent telling this tall tale, as well as how awful the pun is.&nbsp;</p><p>So, now you know. And knowing is half the battle.</p><p>(The other half is violence.)</p>",
